# tidy_baseline.txt — kingdom `tidy` lint baseline.
#
# One entry per over-length function, format: path:function_name:lines
#   path           relative to --root (the same form tidy prints in findings)
#   function_name  the bare identifier after `fn`
#   lines          the function's current measured span (inclusive, fn line to closing brace)
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# The baseline may only SHRINK:
#   - shorten the function, re-run tidy, and lower `lines` to match — never raise it
#   - a function that shrinks to <= 70 lines must have its entry deleted (tidy fails
#     with "stale baseline: ... shrank to N lines" until you do)
#   - a function that grows past its recorded `lines` fails as "stale baseline: ... grew
#     to N lines"; fix the function, don't edit the number upward
#   - a renamed or removed function's leftover entry fails as "matches no function";
#     delete the line
#
# These are illustrative only — copy this file to tidy_baseline.txt and replace every
# entry with your own realm's actual long functions (run tidy once with an empty
# baseline to see what needs listing).

src/pool.zig:Pool:136
src/terminal_detect.zig:detectWith:162
build.zig:build:1918
